# THIS laptop's drone. Copy to config/my-drone.env (gitignored) and fill in.
# flash-drone.ps1 and drone-net.ps1 read it, so you don't have to type the ID every time.
#
# DRONE_ID: 0-30, written on the drone. Must be different from every other drone that shares the
#   router: it decides the drone's IP 192.168.1.(200+ID) and the laptop's IP 192.168.1.(100+ID).
# ESP_TX_PIN / ESP_RX_PIN: the ESP32 GPIO numbers of the serial link to the flight controller,
#   from how YOUR cable is wired (docs/wiring.md). Course default: TX 5, RX 4.
#   ESP_TX_PIN = the ESP32 pad wired to the flight controller's RX.
#   ESP_RX_PIN = the ESP32 pad wired to the flight controller's TX.

DRONE_ID=
ESP_TX_PIN=5
ESP_RX_PIN=4
